# Official guía framework — Creación Digital I–II

> **The live PDF is the institutional contract.** In-repo JSON clones are working copies that must reconcile to those PDFs. Every CV, unit forge, `tracks.yml` hour allocation, and evaluation claim must close to the tables below. Do not invent FE-style 10/30/14 splits. Do not invent competencies or contents.

## Canonical sources (in-repo clones)

| Course | Path | Upstream scrape | PDF (authority) |
| ------ | ---- | --------------- | --- |
| **CD I** | [`cv/guides/1-creacion-digital-i.json`](./cv/guides/1-creacion-digital-i.json) | `unicrawler/output/guides/1-creacion-digital-i.json` | [9729001103.pdf](https://universidadeuropea.es/myfiles/pr/9729001103.pdf) · **2026-27** |
| **CD II** | [`cv/guides/3-creacion-digital-ii.json`](./cv/guides/3-creacion-digital-ii.json) | `unicrawler/output/guides/3-creacion-digital-ii.json` | [9729001108.pdf](https://universidadeuropea.es/myfiles/pr/9729001108.pdf) · **2025-2026** (not yet rolled) |

**Re-sync:** copy from unicrawler only after that scrape matches the live PDF. Prefer PDF if JSON and PDF disagree — flag the conflict, do not silently invent. Provenance of the 2026-08-14 patch: [`cv/README.md`](./cv/README.md).

**Default modality for authoring:** `Modalidad presencial` (Campus Creativo). CD I’s PDF labels the other table **Modalidad online**; CD II still says **Modalidad virtual**. Never mix presencial hours with online/virtual labels.

