## 7. Forge artefact ↔ official activity mapping

| Official activity | Forge artefact | Evidence channel |
| ----------------- | -------------- | ---------------- |
| Clases magistrales · Seminarios · Debates (online: clases virtuales síncronas · Foro) | **B1 Conceptual lesson + deck** | claims, competency map |
| Actividades en talleres y/o laboratorios · Investigaciones y proyectos / Proyectos | **B2 Studio brief** (atelier / contextualised) | process folder, piece IDs, project milestones |
| Resolución de problemas | **B3 Exercise set** (individual, decontextualised) | worked solutions |
| Trabajo autónomo | reading list / self-check | not graded as contact |
| Tutoría · Pruebas | course-level | evaluation table only |

**Do not collapse** talleres/proyectos with resolución de problemas — the guía separates them; that separation is also the individual vs cohort evidence channel for research.

---

## 8. Binding rules for all pedagogical actions

1. Open the matching `cv/guides/*.json` **and** the live PDF **before** writing a CV, unit, track session, or assessment page.  
2. CONTENIDOS anchors and competency codes come from JSON — verbatim.  
3. Hour fields in `tracks.yml` must use the keys in §5. Course-level `formative_hours` must close to 150. Session rows, when forged, must carry **every** contact-forgeable key (not only a generic `duration`).  
4. Evaluation % on student-facing pages must match §6.  
5. Scholarly citations still follow [`grounding/README.md`](./grounding/README.md) (discover vectors → cite Ahmes nodes). Institutional hour/weight claims cite the PDF, not the research vault.  
6. vShowroom synergy is L3 — it may consume CD II portfolio/avatar/AR outputs; it may not rewrite §2 contents.
